---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import BreadcrumbHero from "../components/BreadcrumbHero.astro";
import { site } from "../data/site";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="How Hydraulic Match handles contact details, hydraulic product data and files submitted through RFQ forms."
  currentPath="/privacy"
  noindex
>
  <BreadcrumbHero
    title="Privacy Policy"
    trail={[{ label: "Home", href: "/" }, { label: "Privacy" }]}
    variant="5"
  />
  <article class="hm-policy container">
    <p class="hm-policy__date">Effective: August 2, 2026</p>
    <p class="hm-policy__notice">
      Hydraulic Match is a pre-launch sourcing brand. A verified contracting
      entity is identified in a formal quotation before a transaction. Privacy
      questions and data requests can be sent to <a
        href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a
      >.
    </p>

    <h2>Information we collect</h2>
    <p>
      We collect the contact name, business email, company, phone, destination,
      buyer role, product reference, model code, quantity, application details
      and files you choose to submit. Website security systems may also process
      IP address, browser and request data needed to prevent abuse.
    </p>

    <h2>Why we use it</h2>
    <p>
      We use submitted information to identify the requested component, review a
      possible supply route, communicate with you, prepare a quotation,
      coordinate inspection or shipping when requested, maintain transaction
      records and protect the inquiry service. We do not use uploaded technical
      files for public marketing or model-database content without separate
      permission.
    </p>

    <h2>Technical files and confidential information</h2>
    <p>
      Nameplates, product photos, drawings, datasheets and RFQ lists may contain
      confidential information. Upload only material you are authorized to
      share. Do not submit passwords, payment-card data, government identifiers
      or unrelated personal records. Files are checked for permitted type and
      size, but no internet transfer is risk-free.
    </p>

    <h2>Service providers and supply-chain recipients</h2>
    <p>
      Cloudflare may process website, security and private file-storage data;
      Zoho may process inquiry-email delivery. Relevant technical details may
      be shared with candidate manufacturers, suppliers, inspection providers or
      logistics partners only where needed to answer the inquiry or perform an
      accepted order. Those recipients may be located in China or another
      country involved in the requested supply route. We do not sell inquiry
      data.
    </p>

    <h2>Retention</h2>
    <p>
      Unsuccessful or inactive RFQ records are normally retained for up to 24
      months, and uploaded technical files for up to 12 months. Records tied to
      a quotation, order, warranty, legal duty or dispute may be kept longer for
      the applicable business or legal period. Backup and email copies can take
      additional time to expire. You may request earlier deletion where no
      overriding obligation applies.
    </p>

    <h2>Security controls</h2>
    <p>
      The inquiry endpoint limits file count and size, checks permitted
      extensions and file signatures, uses bot verification when configured, and
      can archive files in private object storage. Access should be limited to
      people involved in quotation and order handling. These controls reduce
      risk but cannot guarantee absolute security.
    </p>

    <h2>Your choices</h2>
    <p>
      To request access, correction or deletion, or to withdraw an inquiry,
      email <a href={`mailto:${site.email}`}>{site.email}</a> with enough information
      to identify the submission. We may need to verify the request and may retain
      records required for fraud prevention, legal compliance, transaction evidence
      or dispute handling.
    </p>

    <h2>Policy changes</h2>
    <p>
      We will update the effective date when this policy changes materially.
      Before launch, the published legal identity, actual service configuration
      and retention operations must be checked against this notice.
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
<style>
  .hm-policy {
    max-width: 900px;
    padding-top: 75px;
    padding-bottom: 100px;
  }
  .hm-policy__date {
    color: #667181;
  }
  .hm-policy__notice {
    padding: 22px 24px;
    border-left: 3px solid var(--color-primary);
    background: #f5f8fc;
  }
  .hm-policy h2 {
    margin: 44px 0 12px;
    font-size: 28px;
  }
  .hm-policy p {
    color: #536071;
    line-height: 1.75;
    font-size: 17px;
  }
  .hm-policy a {
    color: var(--color-primary);
  }
</style>
